id=a52sxq_camera_livefocus_profile
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Portrait (live focus) engines pick the A52 profile
author=kusti420
description=Camera audit 2026-11-14 (9.3.118, real scene: chair at ~1.5 m in front of a window). Portrait never applied the blur: the HAL preview logged "LFP DBG: process fail case depthResult(1)" on every frame and the capture "processBokehForCapture X - error processResult(-1)". The A52s vendor live focus engines (liblivefocus_preview_engine, liblivefocus_capture_engine, libDualCamBokehCapture, lib and lib64) pick their tuning profile (A52Param: llsCond -620, DistanceStart 10, DistanceEnd 8, ...) by looking for "a52" in ro.build.flavor; on this port ro.build.flavor is the S26U value (m3qxxx-user, read by many system apps, so it stays), no profile matched and both engines fell back to "Beyond" (Galaxy S10) parameters ("DeviceParam Loaded as Beyond"). Each library holds exactly one "a52" match string; replace it with "m3q" (same length) so the port's flavor selects the A52 profile. Bind-mount test on 9.3.118 with the real flavor: "DeviceParam Loaded as A52" in both the HAL preview and the capture engine, and the engine reports the real low-light state (depthResult 31, "Too dark."); real scene (chair ~1.5 m): "Capture bokeh effect was applied", DualShot depth map saved.
